+    Each line is written as its bookmark arrives from the lazy cursor, so peak memory does not
+    grow with the collection -- the same shape as ``write_csv``/``write_json`` (SR-019).
+
+    ``join_tags()`` is reused rather than re-sorted, which is what makes FR-042's "identical to
+    the ``tags`` field of ``export --format csv``" true by construction. Escaping is per
+    context: the URL lands in an attribute value, the title and the tag string in element text
+    (FR-043, SR-012).
+    """
+    stream.write(HTML_PROLOGUE)
+    for bookmark in bookmarks:
+        stream.write(
+            f'<li><a href="{_escape_attr(bookmark.url)}">'
+            f"{_escape_text(bookmark.title)}</a>"
+            f" <small>{_escape_text(join_tags(bookmark.tags))}</small></li>\n"
